r={'id':'nz-kvs-kv9-solid-tumor-pilot','title':'Kv9 intratumoral immunotherapy pilot for accessible solid tumors','center':'Kode Veterinary Sciences — New Zealand multicentre pilot','country':'New Zealand','species':['Dog','Cat'],'cancers':['Soft tissue sarcoma','Mast cell tumor','Mammary carcinoma','Melanoma — other','Oral melanoma','Oral squamous cell carcinoma','Squamous cell carcinoma — other','Anal sac adenocarcinoma'],'status':'Recruiting — current official pilot page and owner FAQ','status_confidence':'confirmed_current','available_for_matching':True,'study_type':'treatment','url':primary['url'],'source_url':primary['url'],'contacts':'Kode Veterinary Sciences clinical study team — study@kodevet9.com; referral through the primary veterinarian','funding':'Kv9, treatment appointments and study monitoring visits are covered. Owners pay the initial tumor diagnosis and other veterinarian-recommended tests. Unrelated care, pre-existing conditions and agreed exclusions remain owner-paid; travel coverage is not stated.','funding_status':'Study treatment and monitoring covered; initial diagnosis and other care owner-paid','funding_source':primary['url'],'funding_verified':'2026-10-18','intervention':'Intratumoral Kv9 immunotherapy, usually up to three treatments about two weeks apart, followed by at least nine monitoring visits over two years','treatment_approaches':['immunotherapy'],'requires':{'confirmed':True,'active_treatment_target':True,'measurable':True,'accessible_intratumoral_target':True,'min_tumor_cm':1,'max_tumor_cm':5,'kv9_concurrent_drugs_eligible':True},'excludes':{'concurrent_chemotherapy':True},'owner_prescreen_required':True,'sites':sites,'verified':'2026-10-18','notes':'One current Kv9 pilot, with all eight named treatment centres retained. The official FAQ explicitly accepts dogs and cats; its detailed cancer examples are phrased for dogs, so feline histology and site eligibility require KVS confirmation. Bay of Plenty is location pending and is not represented as an active ninth site. Horse enrollment is outside this catalog. Previous surgery may be accepted if an injectable residual or recurrent tumor remains. Other solid tumors require case-by-case review; no blanket all-cancer or bone-cancer cohort is inferred. The experimental treatment has no guaranteed benefit.','special_requirement':'Pathologist-confirmed cytology or biopsy; accessible tumor approximately 1–5 cm. No concurrent chemotherapy or disallowed immune-modulating medication, but the protocol explicitly permits Apoquel, Cytopoint, Beransa and recent vaccination. Soft tissue sarcoma must not have surface wounds; other tumor types are assessed individually. Residual/recurrent tumors after surgery may qualify if at least 1 × 1 cm remains. Full referral, feline-specific criteria, medication exceptions and site availability require KVS screening.'}
